    <briefdescription>
<para>Implementation for communicate. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Implements <ref refid="classCommunicate_1ac17ede80bd387e5c096fcf9fcb481aee" kindref="member">Communicate::sendRequest</ref>, which allocates a cURL handle and header list, builds the URL, chooses GET or POST through a small lookup table of lambdas, performs the transfer and cleans up. handleResponse registers WriteCallback so incoming bytes are appended to a string, and WriteCallback does that append. Failures are logged and returned as empty optionals instead of thrown exceptions.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: This is where the actual outbound HTTP work happens. Callers get a simple &quot;send this request, give me the body&quot; interface while all the messy libcurl setup, method selection, resource cleanup and error logging stay here. Because every failure is converted to std::nullopt, callers do not need try/catch blocks of their own. Without this file the service-to-service calling code would have to be repeated and carefully cleaned up at every call site.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>libcurl easy API: <ulink url="https://curl.se/libcurl/c/curl_easy_init.html">https://curl.se/libcurl/c/curl_easy_init.html</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>std::function: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/functional/function">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/functional/function</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Lambdas with captures ([&amp;curl, &amp;data]): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/lambda">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/lambda</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>std::optional::value_or: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/value_or">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/value_or</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
